{
 "id": "synthetic-chw-plant-multi",
 "title": "Synthetic chilled-water plant: two chillers, a secondary loop and a tower (generated by CAMBER)",
 "summary": "SYNTHETIC, generated locally by CAMBER (no download, no real building): a primary-secondary chilled-water plant with two equal chillers, a decoupler, a variable-flow secondary loop and one cooling tower, with outdoor dry-bulb and wet-bulb, each chiller's status, power, leaving and entering water and condenser and evaporator approach, the secondary loop's supply, return, setpoint, flow, pump speed and pump power, and the tower's leaving and return water, condenser-water flow and fan speed, every 15 minutes for three summer weeks with a heat wave, as seven plants: well run, both chillers always on, decoupler reverse mixing from low delta-T coils, a fouled condenser on chiller 1, a badly fouled tower pinned at full fan, a moderately fouled tower that holds its setpoint by fan effort, and a near miss.",
 "teaches": [
  "over-staging across two chillers (chiller_staging_fleet), which needs each chiller as its own equipment",
  "a secondary loop whose supply runs warm while both chillers hold their setpoint: decoupler reverse mixing",
  "a fouled condenser read from the chiller's own approach",
  "why a tower's approach shows fouling only at full fan, and fan effort shows it on a controlled tower",
  "a near miss: a plant a little off everywhere that passes every check"
 ],
 "publisher": "CAMBER (generated locally by the user's copy)",
